WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(gentle music)

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.820
- A lot of my clients
and their family members

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.803
live in a constant state of fear.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.220
Thirty years ago, I mean,

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.100
there were very little deportation cases,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.083
and now that is the bulk
of cases that we take.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.430
Many of the cases go through
the Stewart Detention Center,

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.243
and a lot of attorneys
don't take Stewart cases.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.750
I really worry that,

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.270
if I were not in some of my client's lies,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.383
that they would be in a
very difficult situation.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.430
I do what I do because I am an immigrant.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.050
I know how they feel;

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.623
I know what their family
members are going through.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.890
I would hate for someone

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.750
not to have the proper representation

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:59.933
because I know that I'm
really their last hope.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.030
I was born in the Dominican
Republic and, at 12 years old,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.453
my family and I moved
to the United States.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.063
We moved to New York, and
then we moved to Georgia.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.780
I went on to Georgia State University,

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.620
and then I got a chance to work

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.190
at an immigration law
firm as a receptionist,

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.290
and it was really a blessing

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.403
because my uncle was picked up by ICE.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.200
You know, we never thought
that that would be possible

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.583
because we came here with a green card.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.440
Why is ICE picking my uncle up?

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.530
Why is he at Stewart Detention Center

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.343
when he's not here illegally?

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.100
He was detained for almost a year

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.670
until we were finally able
to win the removal case,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.700
and it was at that moment I knew

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.317
that I wanted to become
an immigration attorney.

00:02:11.317 --> 00:02:13.900
(somber music)

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.093
So, how are you?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.090
- I'm scared, I'm really scared.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:24.400
I'm not gonna lie.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.114
I'm scared to be in this place,

00:02:26.114 --> 00:02:28.823
and I'm scared to go back to my country.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.473
Honduras is not a place where
you can live freely, you know?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.940
Not if you're gay and I know for sure

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.950
that if I appeal again,

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.382
they will take longer as well, you know?

00:02:43.382 --> 00:02:44.215
- Yeah.
- And it's probably

00:02:44.215 --> 00:02:46.130
gonna be another year.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.850
- Yeah, no, I understand.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:52.162
I mean this is a very serious,

00:02:52.162 --> 00:02:54.113
serious decision that you have to make.

00:02:55.235 --> 00:02:56.730
- Yes.
- Of course, as a lawyer,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.200
I always want to keep fighting.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.820
- Yes.
- We never really give up--

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.580
- Right.
- But it is at the expense

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.583
of your freedom.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.880
- I would like to say that
I would like to fight,

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.860
because I know that you have
done everything that's possible

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.290
and, like I told you before, I'm so grateful

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.793
to have you as my lawyer.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.840
- We do a lot of these cases pro bono,

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.453
and we have 1,500 active cases.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.913
The majority of my clients
have lived here for decades.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.270
They have built a life here.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:48.563
They pay taxes; they have children here;

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.600
and they have lived crime-free lives,

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.600
and then they get pulled
over for traffic violations.

00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:01.313
And you know, that's how they
end up in ICE detention.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.290
So in order for me to
visit a client at Stewart,

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.393
normally, I have to get up at 4:00 a.m.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.650
It's far away.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.260
It takes us about three
hours, one-way, to get there;

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.470
and for years, Stewart had
the highest deportation rate

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.513
in the country.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.480
It's in the middle of
nowhere, cold and isolated,

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.350
and just very difficult to get access to.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.060
It's difficult to get
access to the clients.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.053
It's difficult for media to get access.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.563
It has a horrible reputation.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:02.790
I hear from my clients all the
time about the mistreatment.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.980
These individuals deserve
that their cases be heard

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:09.800
before a judge, so I
have to fight for them,

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.580
and I have to give them
their day in court,

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.230
and they're grateful for
that, that's what they want.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.800
I've had many cases
where my clients come in

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.607
and they said, "I've
met with five attorneys

00:05:27.607 --> 00:05:29.820
"and they told me that
nothing could be done,"

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.853
and we have been able to win their case.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.410
That's really why I do what I do,

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.190
why I don't take no for an answer.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.550
If a client is willing to
allow me to fight their case,

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.073
I will fight the case till the end.

00:05:48.235 --> 00:05:51.985
(speaks in foreign language)

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:41.525
- You know, I really wish

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:47.380
that the immigration debate
could be more focused

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.703
on the actual people.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.560
I mean, I represent
surgeons, nurses, teachers

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:00.033
who are just here trying to
provide for a better life.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.180
It's really a privilege,
and it's really a blessing

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.193
to do what I do.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.970
I get strength from the cases

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:13.990
that we are able to win.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.140
It definitely brings great joy to my life

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.990
'cause I know I've made a difference.

